## generating video script
2026-02-02 20:48:27 | DEBUG | "./app\services\task.py:86": generate_script - video script: 
Why is pancreatic cancer so deadly? It's called the 'silent killer' because it rarely shows early symptoms. By the time symptoms like jaundice or weight loss appear, the cancer is often already quite advanced, frequently leading to missed opportunities for effective treatment. The difficulty of early diagnosis is the biggest problem.

The aggressive growth of cancer cells is a daunting reality. Pancreatic cancer has a very strong tendency to rapidly infiltrate and metastasize to surrounding organs, blood vessels, and lymph nodes. Once metastasis begins, surgical cure is rarely possible, robbing patients of even hope.

Treatment itself is a continuous series of challenges. A thick fibrous tissue surrounds the tumor, preventing chemotherapy drugs from penetrating effectively. Pancreatic cancer cells rapidly develop resistance to chemotherapy, diminishing the effectiveness of existing treatments, and the development of new therapies is also slow.

Furthermore, the pancreas is hidden deep within the body, surrounded by major blood vessels and organs. This makes surgery itself complex and risky, and extensive resection is difficult due to the crucial functions of the pancreas. All these complex factors combined make pancreatic cancer one of the most dreaded diseases.
