## generating video script
2026-02-03 13:09:35 | DEBUG | "./app\services\task.py:86": generate_script - video script: 
What is the leading cause of death globally? Surprisingly, it's cardiovascular disease. This condition claims millions of lives every year and is considered the primary cause of heart attacks and strokes. While many remain unaware, it's a silent killer that slowly damages our blood vessels. Cardiovascular disease primarily occurs when blood vessels narrow or become blocked due to atherosclerosis. A Westernized diet, lack of physical activity, smoking, and excessive stress are the main causes, and chronic diseases like high blood pressure, high cholesterol, and diabetes further increase the risk. The busy routines and irregular habits of modern individuals are major contributors to heart disease.

Proactive prevention is crucial to protect ourselves from this fatal disease. It's important to manage blood pressure and cholesterol levels through regular health check-ups and to maintain a balanced diet rich in vegetables and fruits. Furthermore, at least 30 minutes of daily aerobic exercise and quitting smoking serve as the strongest shields for cardiovascular health. It shouldn't be dismissed as merely a part of aging. By adopting healthy lifestyle habits now, it can be largely prevented and managed. I hope we can all enjoy healthier lives by starting with small changes for our hearts and sharing this vital information with those around us. Cardiovascular health is not an option; it's a necessity.
